course: dictionary
lesson: 1752
title: Meet the classroom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A classroom is a room in a school where pupils have lessons. It is where you sit at your desk, listen to the teacher, and learn.
explain: Read the words around the word to understand it. «When the head teacher walks into the classroom, pupils stop talking and look up.» The sentence shows a classroom is a place where pupils and teachers are together during the school day.
explain: Classroom also appears in maths. The sentence can be counted: total = classrooms × pupils each. Always check your meaning by putting it into a sentence: "The lesson is in the classroom" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Classroom means a room in a school where pupils have lessons.
fact: Classroom is a noun. Its plural is classrooms.
fact: Maths example: if a school has 6 classrooms and each has 25 pupils, there are 150 pupils in total, because 6 × 25 = 150.
fact: «Air has weight; the air in an ordinary classroom weighs about as much as several children together.»
fact: In a fire drill, pupils line up at the classroom door and walk out calmly.
exercise: What is a classroom? | A bus that takes pupils home | A shop where children buy books | *A room in a school where pupils have lessons | A field where children play football
exercise: «When the head teacher walks into the classroom, pupils stop talking and look up.» Where does this happen? | *In a school room where pupils learn | At a bus stop | In a shop | At home at bedtime
exercise: Copy the word from «Look around a classroom: paper in your exercise book» that names the room where pupils have lessons. | paper | exercise | book | *classroom
test: A school has 6 classrooms and each has 25 pupils. How many pupils are there in total? | 120 | *150 | 160 | 130
test: Which of these is part of school life in a classroom? | Sleeping in a bed | *Lining up at the door for a fire drill | Driving a car to school | Cooking dinner in an oven
exam: Look at «Air has weight; the air in an ordinary classroom weighs about as much as several children together.» According to the sentence, what does the air in a classroom weigh roughly? | As much as a single pencil | As much as one feather | As much as a bus | *As much as several children together
